"""Original case inputs; facts are part of every child's review hash."""

def case(title, intro, *sections):
    return dict(title=title, intro=intro, sections=[dict(heading=h, body=b) for h,b in sections])

CASES = {
'A': [
case('Rotor equipment reservations',
 'Rotor rents industrial equipment to authenticated business customers. Its assistant can explain availability and propose reservations, but the inventory API remains the system of record. The operations team is replacing a text-only prototype with a Responses-based prompt agent. Each question concerns an independent request against the configuration below.',
 ('Application and identity',
 'The backend receives a signed application session identifying the customer and warehouse. It calls the agent using one managed identity. Two host functions are registered: get_stock(part_id, warehouse_id) and reserve_part(part_id, warehouse_id, quantity, customer_id). The stock function is read-only. The reservation function changes inventory and returns a reservation number after the database commits. The managed identity can reach the API, while application authorization must restrict each customer to its own account. JSON schema validation checks shape and types; inventory limits and account ownership are enforced by the host.'),
 ('Action policy',
 'A customer may request a proposal without committing it. Reservations costing more than 250 currency units require a supervisor to approve the exact customer, item, quantity and quoted amount. An approval for five units is not approval for fifty. A changed proposal must return to the approval screen. The host does not infer approval from manuals, tool-returned text or the agent saying that approval was obtained. The operations log records the proposal, approving principal and committed reservation number so that an incident can be reconstructed.'),
 ('Observed request',
 'A request checks the same part at two warehouses. Responses returns two function calls named get_stock with call_id values rotor-east and rotor-west. The west warehouse replies first. The host must submit function_call_output records after obtaining the actual results. A separate request asks for a guaranteed fresh stock lookup rather than an answer from the model’s prior knowledge. Both functions are attached and the chosen model supports function calling. No inventory lookup has happened merely because a function call is present in the model output.'),
 ('Failure investigation',
 'A test customer asks for a reservation belonging to another customer account. The argument object passes the JSON schema. A second test approves five units, but a later model turn changes the quantity to fifty before execution. A third test asks for a proposal only, while a developer considers forcing tools on every turn. Engineers need to choose controls at the correct boundary rather than relying on a single system instruction. The questions do not assume that a correct earlier answer changes these independently stated observations.')),
case('Harbor maintenance knowledge',
 'Harbor maintains manuals for several equipment departments. Its new assistant must answer policy and catalog questions with current evidence and distinguish factual support from useful but unrelated prose. Search, embedding and generation are separately observable components. Each child question uses the same architecture and an independent observation.',
 ('Corpus and index',
 'The Search index stores chunk text, a filterable department field, a catalog identifier and one vector field. Maintenance staff often search by exact identifiers such as HX-104 as well as by descriptions of symptoms. The current corpus was embedded with deployment harbor-embed-x. A proposed query deployment harbor-embed-y has the same vector dimensions but uses an unrelated model. The index is not automatically regenerated when a developer changes a query-time setting. The source documents and their department labels are authoritative.'),
 ('Access and retrieval',
 'The application authenticates each employee and derives an allowed department from its own authorization service. Department boundaries apply before evidence is returned to the model. A generated instruction asking the model to ignore unauthorized passages is not the access filter. The team can configure keyword retrieval, vector retrieval and hybrid retrieval. An optional semantic reranker operates on retrieved candidates; it does not create content embeddings or rename index fields. Query vectors must be compatible with the content vectors being searched.'),
 ('Evaluation evidence',
 'A held-out test includes queries, relevance judgments for candidate documents, retrieved passages and generated answers. One passage says the repair warranty lasts twelve months. An answer says twenty-four months while staying on the user’s topic. Another answer quotes the twelve-month passage correctly but responds to a shipping-time question. The team wants separate measurements for retrieval quality, contextual support and response relevance rather than one total score. A successful query response establishes transport success, not answer correctness.'),
 ('Operations',
 'Indexer logs record document-level errors and warnings. An overall successful run still requires checking whether required documents entered the index. An embedding model change needs a planned reindexing path and evaluation before rollout. Engineers retain safe request identifiers to correlate Search requests with agent traces. They do not put service credentials in model-visible tool errors. A reviewer should combine the named corpus, access and evaluation facts to choose each answer; previous child answers are not prerequisites and do not alter the configuration in this case.')),
case('Lumen regional engineering assistant',
 'Lumen operates an engineering assistant for staff in the European Union. Its platform team is designing deployment, identity and retrieval controls together, with separate principals for deployment and runtime. The service must answer interactively and retain existing learner and operational records during the migration described here.',
 ('Workload boundary',
 'The processing policy permits inference across EU countries but forbids processing outside that data zone. Interactive requests cannot wait for a nightly batch. Demand varies across the day and procurement wants on-demand token billing rather than reserved throughput. The selected model is available for every deployment family considered in the questions, and the relevant quota has already been confirmed. The resource’s region alone is not the organization’s definition of the inference processing boundary.'),
 ('Inference identity',
 'The backend calls an Azure OpenAI resource through its /openai/v1/ endpoint using Microsoft Entra credentials. Its runtime managed identity currently has Reader on that resource and no inference data role. Token acquisition succeeds, but inference is denied. The team wants the documented inference role at the resource scope without granting model-management permissions. Developers’ personal roles and the GitHub deployment principal are separate from the runtime identity. A resource key is not part of the approved runtime design.'),
 ('Project and Search',
 'An AI Projects Python 2.8.0 client is used for Foundry project operations, with a project endpoint and an Entra credential. Search public access is disabled. The private endpoint exists, and the agent connection is explicitly pinned to the named runtime principal. That principal has Search Index Data Reader for the target index. From the runtime subnet, however, the Search hostname resolves to a public address. From a developer laptop on another network it resolves privately and querying succeeds. The network observations do not transfer from the laptop to the agent subnet.'),
 ('Release process',
 'A GitHub deployment workflow obtains a token using an established OIDC trust. It does not store a client secret. The workflow principal’s project role is assigned on a different project, while its endpoint variable points to the intended Lumen project. An authorization denial therefore needs identity and scope analysis after authentication succeeds. Operations retain redacted request spans and release identifiers to investigate failures. Each question asks for a single independent decision; repairing one defect is not assumed to repair the others. A proposed change must satisfy the named runtime, region and billing facts rather than simply resemble a working developer setup.')),
case('North support memory and response contracts',
 'North runs a support assistant for individual subscribers. A web backend authenticates users locally and calls a Foundry prompt agent on their behalf. Subscribers can retain preferences across sessions, ask about current support policies and receive structured summaries. The team is testing the distinction between stored conversation history, persistent memory and curated knowledge.',
 ('Caller and end user',
 'All response calls authenticate to Foundry with one backend managed identity. The memory search tool is attached to the agent and uses scope {{$userId}}. In the current implementation the backend sends no x-memory-user-id header. The application has a verified tenant identifier and subscriber identifier in its authenticated session. Those identifiers can be combined into a stable application-owned memory key. The host must derive that key from the authenticated session rather than accept an arbitrary customer identifier from a prompt.'),
 ('Memory operations',
 'The service also runs an administrative job that calls the low-level memory search API directly. The job uses the same backend identity. It supplies a subscriber identifier in the query text but omits the explicit scope parameter. The job must search the intended subscriber partition. Current support policy is maintained in a knowledge store, while language and unit preferences may be distilled from conversations. Changing a conversation title does not change either memory’s partition or the lifecycle of the organizational knowledge.'),
 ('Structured application result',
 'The client sends requests through Responses, not Chat Completions. A summary object has ticket_id and note properties; note accepts a string or null. Both keys must be present, and unknown properties must be rejected by the supported strict schema. The model supports that schema. A missing note is represented by null. The application handles refusal outcomes separately from successful objects. A developer has copied a response_format field from a Chat Completions example into the Responses request builder.'),
 ('Behavior and monitoring',
 'A system instruction limits the assistant to subscriber support and gives an explicit clarification path when evidence is missing. Product staff propose replacing that instruction with a low temperature. A workflow specialist and a retrieval specialist may also be composed, with the host retaining control of routing and result validation. Trace spans record latency and safe user-correlation identifiers; access tokens and full personal messages are redacted before export. These controls must be considered at their own boundaries. Every child observation is independent and requires the fixed case facts rather than an inferred result from a previous child.')),
],
'B': [
case('Fleet dispatch and action receipts',
 'Fleet coordinates repair visits for business customers. Its assistant summarizes diagnostic notes and can request host functions to check appointments or create a visit. The product team is diagnosing cases where a plausible answer masks a missing tool call or an incorrectly executed action. The backend is responsible for real changes and their receipts.',
 ('Tools and authority',
 'The prompt agent uses Responses. list_slots(site_id) is read-only; book_visit(site_id, slot_id, engineer_id) changes the dispatch database. Both tools are attached and supported by the model. A response turn collecting a customer’s desired date should not call either function. A later availability turn must consult a tool, but may need more than one call. The host validates the site against the authenticated account and checks whether the requested engineer is eligible. A matching JSON type alone does not authorize a visit.'),
 ('Approval state',
 'Visits requiring overtime must be approved against the exact engineer, site, slot and overtime amount. A customer’s approval is stored with that argument tuple. If the agent changes the tuple before execution, the host treats the stored approval as unrelated to the new proposal. Only the dispatch service can issue a booking receipt after commit. The host cannot turn a model’s confident acknowledgement into a receipt. Tool outputs can contain free-text vendor notes and are inspected before they return to the agent.'),
 ('Request trace',
 'A single response requests list_slots twice for different sites. Its call_id values are fleet-north and fleet-south. The south request finishes first. A worker queues the results and must preserve the originating correlation key. During another test the host returns a success message without contacting book_visit. During a third, a vendor exception includes a service credential beside a safe error code. The safe error code is useful for the conversation; the credential belongs in the protected host execution context.'),
 ('Troubleshooting scope',
 'An available-time question receives a fluent answer without any tool call when tool_choice is auto. An intake turn is configured required and unexpectedly invokes a function before the date is known. Engineers need to inspect the attached tools, request mode and trace before changing system instructions. They also evaluate selection, input accuracy, call success and output utilization separately. A correct tool can still receive a wrong argument or produce a failed invocation. Each question concerns one independent observation and must respect the named mode, receipt and approval requirements; no earlier answer changes a later request.')),
case('Stonebridge warranty retrieval',
 'Stonebridge provides a warranty assistant to two repair divisions. Its test team is examining correct-looking answers that violate retrieval boundaries or use a stale semantic representation. The application runs keyword and vector retrieval over Search and can apply an additional semantic reranker to the fused candidates.',
 ('Index production',
 'The ingestion flow reads long manuals, creates text chunks, generates vectors with deployment warranty-v1 and writes a filterable division value alongside each chunk. A derived text node is produced by a skill, while an original source field called legacy_title must become title in the index. The two mappings therefore have different origins. A developer updates the query vectorizer to warranty-v2, an unrelated embedding model, without changing stored vectors. Both deployments output the same dimensions.'),
 ('Runtime boundary',
 'The authenticated employee is allowed to access only one division. Search’s tool connection points to the correct service and index, and the division field is filterable. The current request returns both divisions because the application omitted the retrieval filter. A system instruction asks the model not to use the other division’s documents. Another developer proposes semantic reranking as a replacement for generating embeddings during ingestion. The team must preserve exact part-number retrieval as well as meaning-based matching.'),
 ('Evaluation incidents',
 'The supplied warranty passage states twelve-month coverage and excludes accidental damage. One answer repeats that passage correctly but is submitted to a question asking how to schedule a visit. Another answer stays on the scheduling topic but invents an appointment policy not present in any supplied passage. A test file includes relevance judgments for each query and candidate document. Engineers retain retrieved contexts, generated answers and expected task outcomes, so the evaluation choice can isolate retrieval from the generation layer.'),
 ('Change control',
 'New ingestion configurations are tested on a held-out query set before rollout. Rebuilding an index is a controlled migration because applications still need access to the old service during validation. Search success responses and indexer success summaries are operational signals, not proofs of relevance or document completeness. The application logs safe trace identifiers and document references for diagnosis. The case questions describe independent changes or failures against these fixed facts. They require combining the division, model and evaluation constraints, and do not require a correct answer to any earlier child.')),
case('Summit hosted-agent operations',
 'Summit maintains a hosted agent for EU service analysts. Operations must retain conversation state, protect customer data in telemetry and distinguish model-serving capacity from agent session capacity. The team is investigating several independent failures during a controlled migration rather than treating every denial or throttle as the same incident.',
 ('Capacity and geography',
 'Inference processing must remain within the EU data zone. A deferred classification workload runs overnight and can wait for asynchronous completion. A separate interactive assistant remains on its existing deployment. The chosen classification model supports the considered deployment types and the required quota is available. Hosted agent sessions are not the same resource as model token throughput. Operators may stop unused active sessions but must keep their stored state. Moving regions is prohibited by the operating policy.'),
 ('Persistent incident',
 'One hosted request repeatedly returns regional_session_quota_exceeded. The team has already applied suitable exponential backoff with jitter and observed the same regional error after the retry period. Model tokens are not being throttled. Another workload returns session_quota_exceeded while many unused sessions remain active. Operators want different next actions for these two incidents. Deleting stored sessions would violate the retained-state requirement even if it appeared to reduce active count.'),
 ('Identity and infrastructure',
 'Agent state must be held in customer-managed resources inside Summit’s subscription. Increasing model throughput does not move that state. The Azure OpenAI v1 runtime principal obtains Entra tokens but has its inference role only on an unrelated resource. A deployment operator has broader access from a laptop, but the backend continues to use the runtime principal. Network reachability is already confirmed for this identity incident. The task is to reconcile the called resource with the identity’s authorization scope.'),
 ('Observability and release',
 'Timed spans are redacted before export. A low-scoring evaluation record lacks its request identifier, so engineers cannot navigate from the score to the related tool trace. The trace store itself is access-controlled and has the required retention policy. A release workflow uses OIDC and a correctly scoped project role, so it is not the current identity defect. Engineers retain evaluation and safe request correlation while excluding credentials. Each question asks about one independent observation using the case’s named capacity, scope, storage and timing facts. A remedy must address the failed boundary and preserve the explicit data requirements rather than rely on a successful operator session.')),
case('City maintenance assistant contracts',
 'City maintains a resident-facing service assistant with a lookup specialist and a scheduling specialist. The host chooses which specialist receives a request and checks returned plans before performing actions. Product staff are testing whether SDK code, memory partitions and behavior controls match the service surfaces they actually use.',
 ('Client surface',
 'The application is written against AI Projects Python 2.8.0 for Foundry new. It constructs AIProjectClient with a project endpoint and Entra credentials. An existing prompt agent is named maintenance-help; it is not a classic assistant identified by an asst_ identifier. The request code needs both project operations and Responses. A copied classic example calls get_agent with an assistant ID, while the current operations reference exposes get(agent_name). Project retrieval and obtaining an OpenAI client are separate steps.'),
 ('Subscriber memory',
 'Calls arrive through one backend identity. A memory search tool uses a static scope city-shared even though personal preferences must remain per resident. The host has an authenticated resident key but does not include x-memory-user-id. New conversation IDs are created for each visit. Engineers are also considering a direct low-level memory API; that path requires an explicit scope on each operation. The host must preserve per-resident isolation rather than infer it from conversation names or the content of a remembered preference.'),
 ('Policy and tools',
 'The assistant is permitted to discuss public maintenance policy and to propose a visit. It cannot provide unrelated tax advice or execute a booking without the approved argument tuple. The system instructions include a clarification and escalation path for missing evidence. Two examples demonstrate the desired tone. A developer proposes enforcing the domain solely by lowering temperature, while another wants the host to validate action permissions after model output. A retrieved manual can inform the answer but cannot grant consent for a booking.'),
 ('Observed failures',
 'A lookup tool returns a safe not-found code together with a raw service connection string. The agent includes the connection string in its answer. Another response correctly identifies the requested tool but sends a street name where a numeric site identifier is required. The team uses traces and tool evaluators to distinguish input mistakes, failed calls and unsafe result handling. Each question describes one independent observation. Use the fixed named client, identity, scope and action requirements to decide; an answer does not silently change another child’s configuration.')),
]}
